>e

The Village Green
A trampled circle of grass ringed by a dozen houses like your own. Smoke rises,
unhurried, from one or two chimneys. Your house is to the west, the sandwich hut
stands to the east, and a path runs north to the meadow where the occasional
ship puts down. A track drops away south towards the orchard slope, and two
small paths wander off to the southwest (the Reeve's lodge) and the southeast
(the smokehouse).

>s

The Orchard Slope
A gentle slope of sourberry bushes, planted by someone with ambition and tended
by someone with a scarf. The bushes are low and thorny and heavy with small
purple berries; bees move among them like a committee. The village is back to
the north.

Sourberries cling to the bushes in thorny profusion. 

>take berries
You pick the berries with your sleeves held out of the thorns' way, and tip them
into the basket. The bees allow it, after a short debate.

[The score has just gone up by three points.]

