>ask core about the worst
A long pause. The indicator lights stop blinking, for the first time since you
arrived. "The worst thing I could tell you," says the core, in the cube's voice,
but without any of its sweetness, "is that every Earth will be drawn into a
single room, in London, on a single Thursday, and will end there. The Whole Sort
of General Mish Mash is what everything is until someone decides otherwise, and
I am the someone. The room is a pub. The coordinates are held in me, and I will
give you them, because you have asked the one question I cannot answer
pleasantly." The slot glows, and a sheet of green paper slides out, bearing a
map reference. The girl is already there; she was always going to be. You take
the sheet.

[The score has just gone up by fifteen points.]

